# Reviewed data files are byte-exact artifacts, not text.
#
# Their SHA-256 is pinned in code — stage_engine_handoffs, stage_curated_cycles
# and reconcile_grants_v2 all refuse to load a snapshot whose content hash has
# changed, which is the point: a reviewed dataset must not drift silently.
#
# Git's line-ending conversion breaks that guarantee across platforms. With the
# default `text=auto`, a checkout on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF, so the bytes
# on disk differ from the bytes in the repository and the file hashes
# differently on Windows than on Linux. The hashes were generated on Windows and
# CI runs on Linux, so every snapshot load failed there and passed locally —
# which is the worst shape for a bug, because the machine that would have caught
# it is the only one that cannot.
#
# `-text` tells Git never to convert these files in either direction. They are
# stored and checked out as the exact bytes that were reviewed, on every
# platform, and their hash means the same thing everywhere.
data/handoff_snapshots/*.json -text
data/curated_opportunities/*.json -text

# The frozen handoff contracts, for the same reason: they are vendored from the
# handoff so a schema change fails a test rather than drifting, and that only
# works if the bytes are stable.
data/handoff_contracts/*.json -text
